import{c as i,R as e,S as t}from"./index-Kr1mlcrY.js";import{H as a}from"./heart-QkAG7q5W.js";import{B as o}from"./brain-Cpx4LZne.js";const s=[["path",{d:"M12 6.528V3a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h0",key:"11qiee"}],["path",{d:"M18.237 21A15 15 0 0 0 22 11a6 6 0 0 0-10-4.472A6 6 0 0 0 2 11a15.1 15.1 0 0 0 3.763 10 3 3 0 0 0 3.648.648 5.5 5.5 0 0 1 5.178 0A3 3 0 0 0 18.237 21",key:"110c12"}]],r=i("apple",s),c=[{id:1,title:"10 Simple Ways to Boost Your Heart Health Daily",category:"Cardiology",excerpt:"Small changes in your routine can make a big difference for your heart. From brisk walking to choosing healthy fats, discover how to maintain a strong cardiovascular system.",description:"Your heart works tirelessly to keep you going. Learn how small, daily habits can significantly improve your cardiovascular health and longevity.",fullContent:`Maintaining a healthy heart doesn't always require drastic lifestyle changes. In fact, it's the small, consistent habits that often make the most significant impact over time.

1. Get Moving: Aim for at least 30 minutes of moderate-intensity exercise most days of the week. Even a brisk walk during your lunch break can work wonders.
2. Watch Your Plate: Focus on whole foods, including plenty of fruits, vegetables, and whole grains. Limit saturated fats, trans fats, and excess salt.
3. Manage Stress: Chronic stress is a major contributor to heart issues. Practice relaxation techniques like deep breathing, meditation, or spending time in nature.
4. Prioritize Sleep: Aim for 7-9 hours of quality sleep each night. Poor sleep is linked to higher risks of obesity and heart disease.
5. Stay Hydrated: Water is essential for every bodily function, including heart performance.

By incorporating these simple steps into your daily routine, you're taking proactive measures to ensure your heart remains strong and resilient for years to come.`,author:"Dr. Rajesh Kumar",date:"May 15, 2024",image:"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1505751172876-fa1923c5c528?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=800",icon:e.createElement(a,{className:"w-5 h-5"})},{id:2,title:"Understanding Minds: Mental Wellness in a Fast World",category:"Mental Health",excerpt:"In today's fast-paced environment, taking care of your mental health is as crucial as physical fitness. Discover techniques for mindfulness and stress management.",description:"Mental health is often overlooked, but it is the foundation of our overall well-being. Explore how to navigate modern stress and maintain mental clarity.",fullContent:`In a world that never seems to slow down, prioritizing mental wellness is no longer optional—it's a necessity.

Mental health affects how we think, feel, and act. It also helps determine how we handle stress, relate to others, and make healthy choices.

- Mindfulness Meditation: Just 10 minutes a day of mindful breathing can significantly reduce anxiety levels.
- Digital Detox: Set aside time each day to disconnect from screens and engage with the physical world around you.
- Seek Connection: Humans are social creatures. Maintain strong relationships and don't hesitate to reach out when you need support.
- Physical Activity: Exercise releases endorphins, which are natural mood lifters.

Remember, seeking professional help is a sign of strength, not weakness. At Dwarika Hospital, our mental health experts are dedicated to supporting you through every challenge.`,author:"Ms. Anjali Sharma",date:"May 12, 2024",image:"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544367567-0f2fcb009e0b?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=800",icon:e.createElement(o,{className:"w-5 h-5"})},{id:3,title:"Nutrition Guide: Superfoods for Your Immune System",category:"Nutrition",excerpt:"Fuel your body with the right nutrients to fight off infections. Here are the top 5 superfoods you should include in your daily diet for maximum immunity.",description:"What you eat directly impacts your body's ability to defend itself. Discover the power of superfoods in building a robust immune system.",fullContent:`A strong immune system is your body's first line of defense against illness. Nutrition plays a pivotal role in maintaining that defense.

Top 5 Superfoods for Immunity:
1. Citrus Fruits: Packed with Vitamin C, which is thought to increase the production of white blood cells.
2. Garlic: Contains heavy concentrations of sulfur-containing compounds, such as allicin, which aid in immune support.
3. Spinach: Not only rich in Vitamin C, but also packed with numerous antioxidants and beta carotene.
4. Yogurt: Look for yogurts that have "live and active cultures" to stimulate your immune system.
5. Turmeric: This bright yellow spice has been used for years as an anti-inflammatory in treating both osteoarthritis and rheumatoid arthritis.

Eating right is a great start, but don't forget that a balanced diet coupled with regular exercise and adequate sleep is the ultimate recipe for health.`,author:"Ms. Anjali Sharma",date:"May 10, 2024",image:"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1490645935967-10de6ba17061?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=800",icon:e.createElement(r,{className:"w-5 h-5"})},{id:4,title:"Modern Diagnostics: The Role of AI in Early Detection",category:"Technology",excerpt:"Artificial Intelligence is revolutionizing how we detect diseases. Learn about the latest diagnostic tools at Dwarika Hospital that save lives through early intervention.",description:"The integration of AI in healthcare is saving lives by identifying risks before symptoms even appear. See how we use technology to protect your health.",fullContent:`At Dwarika Hospital, we are at the forefront of medical technology. Artificial Intelligence (AI) is transforming diagnostics by providing unparalleled accuracy and speed.

- Predictive Analysis: AI algorithms can analyze patient data to predict potential health risks years in advance.
- Enhanced Imaging: Our AI-powered radiology tools can spot abnormalities in X-rays and MRIs that might be invisible to the human eye.
- Personalized Medicine: AI helps us tailor treatments specifically to your genetic makeup and health history.

The future of healthcare is here, and it's smarter, faster, and more life-saving than ever before.`,author:"Dr. Rajesh Kumar",date:"May 05, 2024",image:"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1576091160550-217359f4ecf8?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=800",icon:e.createElement(t,{className:"w-5 h-5"})},{id:5,title:"Post-Surgery Care: A Comprehensive Recovery Guide",category:"Surgery",excerpt:"Recovery doesn't end in the operation theater. Follow these essential steps for a smooth post-operative journey and faster healing at home.",description:"Healing is a process that requires patience and proper care. Learn the best practices for recovering comfortably after surgery.",fullContent:`Surgery is just the first step on your path to recovery. What you do after you leave the hospital is just as important as the procedure itself.

- Follow Instructions: Always adhere strictly to the medication and activity guidelines provided by your surgeon.
- Monitor Your Body: Keep an eye on the incision site for any signs of infection, such as increased redness or swelling.
- Nutrition and Rest: Your body needs energy to heal. Eat protein-rich foods and ensure you get plenty of rest.
- Gradual Activity: Don't rush back into heavy lifting or intense exercise. Follow your physical therapy plan if one was prescribed.

Our care team is always available to answer your questions during your recovery at home.`,author:"Dr. Rajesh Kumar",date:"April 28, 2024",image:"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1584515933487-779824d29309?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=800",icon:e.createElement(t,{className:"w-5 h-5"})},{id:6,title:"Dental Hygiene: More Than Just a Bright Smile",category:"General",excerpt:"Oral health is a window to your overall well-being. Discover the connection between gum health and systemic diseases you might not know about.",description:"Your mouth is the gateway to your body. Discover why brushing and flossing are critical for your heart and brain health as well.",fullContent:`Good dental hygiene is about more than just avoiding cavities. Research has shown that oral health is deeply connected to your overall systemic health.

- Heart Health: Gum disease (periodontitis) has been linked to an increased risk of heart disease and stroke.
- Diabetes Management: People with diabetes are more susceptible to gum infections, and gum disease can make it harder to control blood sugar levels.
- Brain Health: Some studies suggest that the bacteria from gum disease can travel to the brain, potentially contributing to Alzheimer's disease.

Regular check-ups and a solid at-home routine are your best defense. Visit our dental department for personalized oral care.`,author:"Ms. Anjali Sharma",date:"April 20, 2024",image:"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1588776814546-1ffce47267a5?auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=800",icon:e.createElement(a,{className:"w-5 h-5"})}];export{c as B};
